<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea to import 63 mln bbls of crude oil in May.</title>
<headline>S.Korea to import 63 mln bbls of crude oil in May.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean oil refiners plan to import 63 million barrels of crude oil this month against an estimated 67 million barrels last month, a ministry official said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Crude oil imports will decline this month because of maintenance shutdowns,&quot; the ministry official in charge of crude imports told Reuters.</p>
<p>LG-Caltex Oil Corp has its No 2 130,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) crude distilation unit closed until May 14 and Ssangyong Oil Refining Co has its No 2 150,000 bpd unit closed until June 1.</p>
<p>Hanwha Energy Co plans to shut down its No 2 200,000 bpd unit on May 28 for a little less than a month.</p>
<p>This month's scheduled crude imports still represent a sharp increase from the 52 million barrels of crude bought in May 1996.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
